# Testing — printf-toto

## Scope

The Makefile `test` target builds and runs **`build/tests/test_core`** (or `build/tests/test_core.exe` on Windows).

Tests cover **pure helpers** only (escape expansion, single-conversion formatting into a buffer, argument-consumption / reuse accounting). There are **no** subprocess/integration tests in-tree; the full CLI format walk is not unit-tested end-to-end.

## Layout

| File | Role |
|------|------|
| `tests/test_runner.c` | `main()` — invokes all suites in fixed order |
| `tests/test_*.c` / `.h` | One scenario per pair; headers declare the test function for `test_runner.c` |

Suggested first scenarios (names may vary; keep one concern each):

- Escape: `\n` / `\t` / `\\` expand correctly
- Literal `%%` → single `%`
- `%s` / `%d` (or `%x`) conversion into a stack buffer
- Arg consumption count used for format reuse
- Unsupported / out-of-scope conversion: document expected reject or skip behaviour if a helper exposes it

One scenario per `.c` / `.h` pair; headers declare the test function for `test_runner.c`.

## Framework

- No external framework — plain C with `<assert.h>`.
- Each case prints `PASS: <descriptive name>` on success.
- `assert()` failure → `abort()` → non-zero exit from `make test`.

## Build (from `Makefile`)

Objects and the test binary live under `build/tests/`:

```makefile
TEST_CORE := build/tests/test_core
# $(TEST_BUILD_DIR)/%.o ← tests/%.c
# link $(TEST_CORE) from $(TEST_OBJS)
test: $(TEST_CORE)
	./$(TEST_CORE)
```

Helpers under test come from `#include` of the relevant `printf_toto_*.h` (and any `static inline` in headers) — **prefer not linking full `src/*.c`** when the API is header-testable; if a helper lives only in a `.c`, link that one object, not the whole CLI.

## Required coverage themes

1. Escape expansion produces the expected bytes and length.
2. A basic string conversion (`%s`) matches the argument bytes.
3. A basic integer conversion (`%d` or `%x`) matches expected text.
4. `%%` yields a single percent character.
5. Arg-consumption / reuse accounting returns the expected count for a simple format.

## Adding tests

- Add `tests/test_<name>.c` + `.h`, declare runner function in `.h`, call from `test_runner.c`, append to `TEST_SRCS` in `Makefile`.
- Keep tests allocation-free where practical; stack buffers only.

## Manual smoke tests (not automated)

After `make`:

```sh
./build/printf-toto --version
./build/printf-toto --help
./build/printf-toto 'Hello\n'
./build/printf-toto '%s\n' one two three
./build/printf-toto '%d 0x%x\n' 255 255
./build/printf-toto '%s\n' hello | head -n 1
# Interactive long output + Ctrl+C — expect exit 130; terminal stays responsive
```
